00:10:23.074 --> 00:10:24.740
JOSHUA HASLETT: Well,
thank you Daryush.

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:28.370
I can't say how excited
we are to be here today,

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:30.920
working with Google to
really transform the customer

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:33.860
experience and deliver
something new, something

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:37.654
we call the intelligent
customer experience.

00:10:37.654 --> 00:10:40.490
Mitel's been in
business for 45 years

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:42.830
and our focus is delivering
seamless communications

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:45.080
and collaboration and
really helping businesses

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.860
communicate more effectively.

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:49.610
We have over 70 million
end users of our technology

00:10:49.610 --> 00:10:51.404
around the world
and we're number two

00:10:51.404 --> 00:10:53.570
in Contact Center for total
contact centers deployed

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:57.050
globally, with more
than 25,000 businesses

00:10:57.050 --> 00:11:00.606
and trusting their customer
experience to Mitel Solutions.

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:05.480
Our expectations
are changing and I'm

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:08.690
sure you're aware of this
just as much as I am.

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:11.150
Most of us want to
self-serve today.

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:14.986
We want to be able to do through
our app or on the website,

00:11:14.986 --> 00:11:16.610
find the information
we're looking for,

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:18.650
transact the way we
want to transact,

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:21.500
and we want that to be
able to work on our time,

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:24.440
on our schedule,
and from our device.

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:26.690
And as a matter
of fact, Synthetix

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:30.830
has identified that 90% of us
will go to a company's website

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:33.440
before we'll call that company.

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:37.770
So to me, that means anytime
we're calling a company,

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:39.750
it's an exception.

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:44.310
It's a missed opportunity for
a good customer experience.

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:47.280
And how important is
customer experience anyway?

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:51.660
Well, Walker has identified that
by 2020, customer experience

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:55.330
will be more important
than product or price.

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:56.790
So it's key that
we figure out how

00:11:56.790 --> 00:12:00.390
to re-innovate and digitally
transform our businesses.

00:12:00.390 --> 00:12:02.500
Let's take Tesla, for instance.

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:07.210
They've completely disrupted
the auto ownership experience.

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:09.670
And we know them all
for electric vehicles,

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:12.630
but did you know that they
can do over-the-air updates?

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:16.020
Push things like ludicrous
speed or autopilot

00:12:16.020 --> 00:12:18.840
after you've rolled the
car out of the dealership?

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:21.360
Secondly, they can
do remote diagnostics

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:23.760
and they can roll a mobile
technician to your site

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:26.280
to come do repairs and service.

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:28.290
I would say it's these things--

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:29.850
these long-tail
differentiators--

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:32.400
that will in the
end, be the brand

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:33.840
that people know about Tesla.

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:35.580
And they're way ahead
on the technology

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:38.320
from their competition.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:41.760
That's why we're re-imagining
the customer experience,

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:44.820
to bring that intelligent
customer experience to all

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:47.400
the companies that use
Mitel Solutions because we

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:49.950
want them to be able to
transform their businesses,

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.130
as well.

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:54.210
So we're combining
Mitel's 45-year history

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:57.280
of understanding how
businesses communicate

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:59.680
both with omnichannel
contact center and the way

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:03.160
that we do complex routing
rules and combining

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:07.810
that with Google's
Contact Center Cloud AI.

00:13:07.810 --> 00:13:09.820
The first is analytics.

00:13:09.820 --> 00:13:12.430
So we do a lot of contact center
business and the key thing

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:15.340
that we typically do
is focus contact center

00:13:15.340 --> 00:13:17.110
metrics internally.

00:13:17.110 --> 00:13:20.087
We help the business understand
how efficient their agents are.

00:13:20.087 --> 00:13:21.670
You heard Daryush
say how expensive it

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:22.915
is to run a contact center.

00:13:22.915 --> 00:13:24.790
That's why the metrics
are focused on keeping

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:26.620
those agents efficient.

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:31.660
But I would say that with AI, we
need to start to look outward.

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.930
It's not so much more about how
do you run efficient agents,

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:37.960
it's about how do you take
those exceptions when people

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:39.460
are calling in
your contact center

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:41.740
and do something smart with it?

00:13:41.740 --> 00:13:44.140
So the ability to
use topic modeler

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:46.510
allows us to take a look at
the information about why

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:49.570
your customers are calling and
help you improve your products

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:52.370
and solutions.

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:54.370
The second is virtual agent.

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:56.110
If we all want to
self-serve, then it

00:13:56.110 --> 00:13:58.750
makes sense that an
always-on agent that

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:00.760
can get us the answers
that we're looking for

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:02.770
would be very helpful.

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:06.440
So with the virtual agent
capability from Google,

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:08.640
we're able to connect
the customer directly

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:11.590
to the knowledge base
inside the organization.

00:14:11.590 --> 00:14:14.370
This allows us to help
that customer get answers

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.830
to their questions in
real-time, with the most

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:20.110
up-to-date information
that's available to them.

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:22.110
And then, of course, when
we go to a live agent,

00:14:22.110 --> 00:14:23.776
we want to make sure
that the customer's

00:14:23.776 --> 00:14:25.980
context of the conversation
with the virtual agent

00:14:25.980 --> 00:14:27.124
is maintained.

00:14:27.124 --> 00:14:29.040
So we're going to pass
that whole conversation

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:32.100
to the live agent, make sure
they understand the context,

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:35.100
and then we're going to keep
the AI in the conversation

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:40.460
to help coach and do research
for that agent in real-time.

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:44.260
Now the same way that Google is
democratizing AI and bringing

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:46.420
that to all of us
as enterprises,

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:47.920
Mitel wants to make
sure that we can

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:51.550
take the capabilities of the
Contact Center AI components

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:54.490
and bring them to all
verticals-- industries--

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:57.410
and make sure that all size
businesses can deploy this.

00:14:57.410 --> 00:15:00.670
So we've integrated it directly
into our CloudLink platform.

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:03.760
It's a cloud-born, native
microservice architecture

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:07.000
that's global, that allows us to
securely connect to the contact

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:09.520
centers that our customers
run, either hosted

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:13.550
in cloud or in their
on-site deployments.

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:16.400
So let's talk about
analytics for a second.

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:20.150
We took a look at why our
customers are calling us.

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:21.920
So in the Mitel
sales support queue,

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:24.380
we ran more than
20,000 call records

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:27.830
through the topic modeler
engine and we took analysis

00:15:27.830 --> 00:15:29.780
on what was coming in.

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:32.300
We identified when we
had a product launch,

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:35.630
we actually had a
migration licensing problem

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:38.030
and we found that
through the signal

00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:41.030
here that you see on the
green line on the graph, that

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:43.130
shows that we had
upgrade in software

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:46.470
as a high component for
why people were calling in.

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:48.880
Now we were able to put
a migration fix in place

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:50.630
and you can see that
green line trend down

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:53.180
rather rapidly
after that was done.

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:55.100
This is how we were
able to improve

00:15:55.100 --> 00:16:00.490
our experience for our
resellers and for our customers.

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:02.250
Now, we're working
with other companies

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:04.252
to make sure that we
validate this technology.

00:16:04.252 --> 00:16:06.210
We want to make sure that
it's simple to deploy

00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:07.980
and easy to on board.

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:11.250
So Acendas Vacations,
Acendas Travel

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:13.094
is helping us to work
through some of this.

00:16:13.094 --> 00:16:14.760
And as a matter of
fact, Rodney Pattison

00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:16.970
is here with us today--
the CTO of Acendas.

00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:18.900
And the key things
that he's excited about

00:16:18.900 --> 00:16:21.180
with using AI in
his business is how

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:24.150
to personalize the
interactions for his customers,

00:16:24.150 --> 00:16:25.440
enhanced support--

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:28.176
extending his hours and making
that interaction better--

00:16:28.176 --> 00:16:30.300
and then providing his
advisors with more effective

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:33.750
means to be very good in that
consultative vacation planning

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:35.220
that they do.

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:37.200
So without further ado,
let's go to a demo.

00:16:44.760 --> 00:16:47.304
So I'm on Acendas'
vacation website here

00:16:47.304 --> 00:16:49.220
and you'll notice that
there's many categories

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:49.928
on their website.

00:16:49.928 --> 00:16:51.590
They've got great information--

00:16:51.590 --> 00:16:54.570
advisors that are experts in
destination for this luxury

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:57.660
vacation travel, destinations
that I can choose from,

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:58.860
experiences.

00:16:58.860 --> 00:17:00.330
They've even got
a really good blog

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:02.040
that's very rich with content.

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:04.230
The problem is as a
customer, I'm not really sure

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:05.172
where to start.

00:17:05.172 --> 00:17:06.630
I'm not sure what
my vacation needs

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:08.379
to be so I want to
talk to an advisor that

00:17:08.379 --> 00:17:10.284
can help me through this.

00:17:10.284 --> 00:17:11.700
So on their website,
I see there's

00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:13.650
a number of different
ways to contact them.

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:15.359
I can come in
through a voice call.

00:17:15.359 --> 00:17:16.569
I can email them.

00:17:16.569 --> 00:17:19.294
But in this case, I
want to do a live chat.

00:17:19.294 --> 00:17:21.710
So I'm going to give them a
little of my information here.

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:30.292
And while this is
queuing up, I'm

00:17:30.292 --> 00:17:32.750
able to look at a little of
the information on the website.

00:17:37.442 --> 00:17:38.900
Make sure our
internet connection's

00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:40.066
working smoothly here today.

00:17:43.070 --> 00:17:45.380
So now I'm greeted by Marisol--

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:47.080
the Acendas travel bot.

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:49.520
And Marisol can help guide
me through my preferences,

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:51.332
experiences I'm looking for.

00:17:51.332 --> 00:17:53.540
So in this case, I'm interested
in a family vacation.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:06.690
And I think based
upon my kids' age,

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:08.220
they like to go
play at the beach

00:18:08.220 --> 00:18:09.780
so maybe we'll go to Hawaii.

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:20.560
Now Marisol takes me through an
understanding of my preferences

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:22.630
and at that time,
it's looking at what

00:18:22.630 --> 00:18:24.790
advisors in the back
end are available that

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:29.090
can help me with my
consultative vacation planning.

00:18:29.090 --> 00:18:30.650
I think I'll just
relax this time.

00:18:39.364 --> 00:18:40.780
So at this point,
Marisol is going

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:44.920
to give me to an agent that can
help me with this interaction.

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:47.950
Turns out, Ahmed's the right
person for me to talk to.

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:50.440
So just like I mentioned,
we passed the entire script

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:54.070
of the bot interaction with the
customer right to the agent.

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:57.010
So as Ahmed, I can get the
understanding of the customers

00:18:57.010 --> 00:18:57.520
context--

00:18:57.520 --> 00:18:59.960
where they want to go,
who the customer is--

00:18:59.960 --> 00:19:01.415
and at this point,
I can say, I'll

00:19:01.415 --> 00:19:03.290
help you with your
Hawaiian vacation travels.

00:19:06.534 --> 00:19:07.200
If I could type.

00:19:24.460 --> 00:19:26.660
So that we're staying in
stream right back and forth

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:28.991
with the customer, same
in the bot interaction.

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:39.322
And now we'll see
suggestions coming in.

00:19:39.322 --> 00:19:41.280
So I mentioned the AI
stays in the conversation

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:43.530
and we start feeding the
agent real information that's

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:45.116
pertinent to that conversation.

00:19:45.116 --> 00:19:46.740
So the first article
that comes up here

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:49.290
is Hawaiian Islands Travel
for Families, which is

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:50.641
exactly what I had asked for.

00:19:50.641 --> 00:19:52.890
So now I can take a look at
some of the Acendas travel

00:19:52.890 --> 00:19:53.550
information.

00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:55.550
I can see that Maui is a
good place for families

00:19:55.550 --> 00:19:56.510
that want to relax.

00:19:56.510 --> 00:19:59.610
Oahu's a good place for the
classic Hawaii experience.

00:19:59.610 --> 00:20:01.350
I think Maui sounds good.

00:20:01.350 --> 00:20:03.960
Now at the same
time, as an agent,

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:06.841
I can pass this information
right to the customer

00:20:06.841 --> 00:20:08.340
so that they can
look for themselves

00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:10.631
about that information and
they can be guided, as well.

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:15.710
So I'm going to go ahead
and end this interaction

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:18.375
and we're going to go
into a voice interaction.

00:20:38.337 --> 00:20:41.150
MARISOL: Hello, thank you for
calling Acendas Vacations.

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:43.370
I'm Marisol, the
Acendas travel bot.

00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:45.855
Please tell me what type of
